r evidence to confirm metabolic vs. autoimmune origin", "Stress-Induced Hyperglycemia (e.g., sepsis): No fever or leukocytosis to support infectious cause"], "alarm_features": ["Marked hyperglycemia (>500 mg/dL)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Endocrine Tumors with Hyperglycemic and Cutaneous Features", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.361681136543015, "posterior": 0.3005657128802164, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["The subacute multisystem presentation provides minimal support for paraneoplastic syndromes (B1) due to the lack of classic glucagonoma rash, but does not excl…"], "evidence_against": ["The absence of glucagonoma-specific features weakly against endocrine tumors (B1) as the primary mechanism but does not definitively exclude them."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, "interrupt_relevance": 0.6, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "etiology", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Insulin Resistance Syndromes", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.3841505524861879, "posterior": 0.31923833729605644, "danger": 0.4, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Obesity supports insulin resistance (B2), but the absence of acanthosis nigricans and the presence of an atypical rash slightly reduce its likelihood."], "evidence_against": ["The painful rash is inconsistent with typical insulin resistance manifestations (B2), weakly reducing its likelihood."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.3, "interrupt_relevance": 0.2, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Autoimmune Beta Cell Destruction", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.21951460142067877, "posterior": 0.3283594326473723, "danger": 0.6, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Abdominal pain and malaise provide moderate support for autoimmune beta cell destruction (B3) as a systemic process, despite not being classic type 1 diabetes …"], "evidence_against": ["The absence of classic type 1 diabetes symptoms weakly against autoimmune beta cell destruction (B3) as the primary mechanism."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.3, "interrupt_relevance": 0.5, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["type 1 diabetes mellitus"]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Hypercortisolism-Related Disorders", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "reopened", "prior": 0.03465370955011839, "posterior": 0.05183651717635484, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Absence of Cushing's syndrome skin changes strongly refutes hypercortisolism as a safety concern."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 3.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.2, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "etiology", "representative_diseases": []}}, "frontier": ["B1", "B2", "B3", "B4"], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the subacute onset with multisystem involvement (rash, gastrointestinal symptoms, hyperglycemia) argue for paraneoplastic syndromes despite the absence of classic glucagonoma rash (necrolytic mi…", "summary": "The subacute multisystem presentation provides minimal support for paraneoplastic syndromes (B1) due to the lack of classic glucagonoma rash, but does not exclude them."},